From a0793260a9cd668f536e09812cf671e58420973d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xiongchenyu <xiongchenyu6@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:31:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] guest: allocate managed-memory backing under a GPU the
 process registered

cuMemAllocManaged returned CUDA_ERROR_UNKNOWN (999) on every GPU except
the host's first one.  Measured on 615.78.08, 2x RTX 4090, both GPUs
exposed to an Ubuntu 24.04 guest (tests/repro/uvm_managed_repro.c):

  CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0    ALL OK
  CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1    FAIL rc=999
      nvkvm: uvm fallback: MAP_EXTERNAL_ALLOCATION ... nvstatus=0x26
  CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1  FAIL rc=999, same nvstatus

and with only the host's second GPU given to the VM (cgroup denies
/dev/nvidia0) the fallback failed one step earlier, at "build RM object
tree", because it opens /dev/nvidia0 unconditionally.

Two causes, both in the managed-memory fallback (nvkvm_uvm_ext.c):

1. The private RM tree used deviceId 0 unconditionally, on the stated
   assumption that the device is "an allocation context, not a
   placement".  It is a placement for UVM: set_ext_gpu_map_location()
   (uvm_map_external.c) looks up the OWNING GPU of the memory, and for an
   RM sysmem object that is the GPU of the device it was allocated under;
   if that GPU is not registered on the va_space the map fails with
   NV_ERR_INVALID_DEVICE ("This is a local or peer allocation, so the
   owning GPU must have been registered").  A process whose only context
   is on GPU 1 never registers GPU 0.

   Now the tree is built under a GPU the fd registered: its UUID is
   resolved to RM's deviceInstance with three NV0000 controls that are
   already in the allowlist (GET_ATTACHED_IDS 0x201,
   GET_UUID_FROM_GPU_ID 0x275, GET_ID_INFO_V2 0x205), and to the
   /dev/nvidiaN to open from the host `information` file's "GPU UUID:" /
   "Device Minor:" lines, which discovery now records next to the BDF.
   The node matters: deviceConstruct() refuses NV01_DEVICE_0 with
   NV_ERR_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS unless osIsGpuAccessible(), i.e. unless
   the calling process holds an fd for THAT GPU's device file.

2. The per-GPU mapping list came from UVM_REGISTER_GPU.  Every entry is
   resolved with uvm_va_space_get_gpu_by_uuid_with_gpu_va_space(), and a
   GPU that is registered but has no GPU VA space fails the whole call
   with NV_ERR_INVALID_DEVICE.  libcuda registers every visible GPU but
   creates a VA space per context, so CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 with one
   context hit it.  The list now comes from UVM_REGISTER_GPU_VASPACE, and
   the owner is preferably taken from that list too.

Known limit, unchanged in kind: the range is mapped on the GPUs that have
a VA space when it is created; a context created later on another GPU
does not see earlier managed allocations.

After (same host, same guest):

  CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 / 1 / 0,1 / 1,0   ALL OK (1048576/1048576)
  tests/validate.sh: cuda_managed_alloc PASS, cuda_managed_coherence PASS
  (3 CPU<->GPU cycles verified); 30/37 PASS vs 29/37 before.  The
  remaining failures are graphics=off (nvidia-modeset absent, Vulkan
  device, GL draw).

No QEMU change and no allowlist change.  The control commands DENYed
during these runs were audited against open-gpu-kernel-modules 615.78.08
and none is on the managed-memory path; all stay denied:

  0x2080019f NV2080_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_SKYLINE_INFO
             OUT-only fixed table (9 x skyline + validEntries), handler
             zeroes params and bounds validEntries by the array size;
             NON_PRIVILEGED.  Benign MIG topology query; nothing needs it.
  0x2080220b NV2080_CTRL_CMD_RC_ENABLE_WATCHDOG
             no params, but MUTATES per-GPU state (krcWatchdogChangeState
             RMAPI_ENABLE_REQUEST) shared with every host client on that
             GPU; flags NON_PRIVILEGED|GPU_LOCK_DEVICE_ONLY.  Deny.
  0x20802a0c NV2080_CTRL_CMD_CE_GET_LCE_SHIM_INFO
             { in ceEngineType; out shimInstance, shimLocalLceIdx },
             ROUTE_TO_PHYSICAL (flat GSP RPC), NON_PRIVILEGED.  Benign;
             not needed.
  0x00003d0e NV0000_CTRL_OS_UNIX_CMD_MEMACCT_GET_LIMITS
             { NvS32 cgroupFd; out count, limits[32] }.  cgroupFd != -1
             is resolved with cgroup_get_from_fd() in the CALLING
             process's fd table -- a guest-chosen fd number interpreted
             on the host -- and the reply enumerates every attached host
             GPU's id and memory-accounting limits, including GPUs not
             given to the guest.  If ever needed, gate it with a bounded
             check (cgroupFd == -1 only) in nvkvm_isolate_handlers.c, not
             a bare row.
  0x00003d0f NV0000_CTRL_OS_UNIX_CMD_MEMACCT_GET_IMPL
             OUT-only NvU32; harmless, but libcuda treats NOT_SUPPORTED as
             "no accounting" and works, so no row without a consumer.
  0x00730102 NV0073_CTRL_CMD_SYSTEM_GET_NUM_HEADS
             display class; graphics-only, out of scope for compute.
---
 src/guest/nvkvm.h          |   9 +-
 src/guest/nvkvm_hostfile.c |  40 ++++++
 src/guest/nvkvm_uvm_ext.c  | 247 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 258 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/guest/nvkvm.h b/src/guest/nvkvm.h
index 686864f..78954ad 100644
--- a/src/guest/nvkvm.h
+++ b/src/guest/nvkvm.h
@@ -282,7 +282,7 @@ struct nvkvm_uvm_fd_state {
 	 */
 	struct mutex     ext_lock;
 	struct nvkvm_fd_ctx *ext_ctl;   /* private /dev/nvidiactl handle     */
-	struct nvkvm_fd_ctx *ext_dev;   /* private /dev/nvidia0, REGISTER_FD */
+	struct nvkvm_fd_ctx *ext_dev;   /* private /dev/nvidiaN, REGISTER_FD */
 	__u32            ext_h_client;
 	__u32            ext_h_device;
 	__u32            ext_h_subdev;
@@ -367,6 +367,7 @@ struct nvkvm_inflight {
 /* "DDDD:BB:DD.F" — a PCI BDF string as it appears under
  * /proc/driver/nvidia/gpus/.  Matches NVKVM_BDF_LEN on the QEMU side. */
 #define NVKVM_BDF_STRLEN  12
+#define NVKVM_UUID_STRLEN 40   /* "GPU-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx" */
 
 struct nvkvm_state {
 	/* Device registration */
@@ -383,6 +384,12 @@ struct nvkvm_state {
 	 * BDF, not the guest slot — so the synthetic proc tree has to be named
 	 * with these.  Filled by nvkvm_hostfile_discover_gpus(). */
 	char           gpu_bdf[NVKVM_MAX_GPUS][NVKVM_BDF_STRLEN + 1];
+	/* The same `information` body's "GPU UUID:" ("GPU-" + 36) and
+	 * "Device Minor:" lines.  The minor is the host's, and QEMU maps guest
+	 * /dev/nvidiaN to host /dev/nvidiaN, so it is also the guest node that
+	 * reaches this GPU.  -1 / "" when the line was absent. */
+	char           gpu_uuid[NVKVM_MAX_GPUS][NVKVM_UUID_STRLEN + 1];
+	int            gpu_minor[NVKVM_MAX_GPUS];
 	unsigned int   uvm_major;
 	dev_t          uvm_devno;
 	struct cdev    uvm_cdev;
diff --git a/src/guest/nvkvm_hostfile.c b/src/guest/nvkvm_hostfile.c
index 5caa3e7..cae9b96 100644
--- a/src/guest/nvkvm_hostfile.c
+++ b/src/guest/nvkvm_hostfile.c
@@ -285,6 +285,45 @@ static bool nvkvm_parse_bus_location(const char *buf, size_t len, char *out)
 	return false;
 }
 
+/* Copy the value after `key` (leading blanks skipped, up to end of line) into
+ * out[0..cap-1], NUL-terminated.  Returns its length, or -1 if absent. */
+static int nvkvm_parse_field(const char *buf, size_t len, const char *key,
+			     char *out, size_t cap)
+{
+	const size_t klen = strlen(key);
+	size_t i, n = 0;
+
+	for (i = 0; i + klen <= len; i++) {
+		if (memcmp(buf + i, key, klen))
+			continue;
+		i += klen;
+		while (i < len && (buf[i] == ' ' || buf[i] == '\t'))
+			i++;
+		while (i < len && buf[i] != '\n' && buf[i] != '\0' && n + 1 < cap)
+			out[n++] = buf[i++];
+		out[n] = '\0';
+		return (int)n;
+	}
+	return -1;
+}
+
+/* "GPU UUID:" and "Device Minor:" of one `information` body.  Absence is not
+ * fatal -- only the managed-memory fallback uses them, and it fails cleanly
+ * without them (nvkvm_uvm_ext.c, ext_owner_gpu). */
+static void nvkvm_parse_identity(const char *buf, size_t len, int idx)
+{
+	char minor[12];
+	unsigned int m;
+
+	nvkvm.gpu_minor[idx] = -1;
+	if (nvkvm_parse_field(buf, len, "GPU UUID:", nvkvm.gpu_uuid[idx],
+			      sizeof(nvkvm.gpu_uuid[idx])) != NVKVM_UUID_STRLEN)
+		nvkvm.gpu_uuid[idx][0] = '\0';
+	if (nvkvm_parse_field(buf, len, "Device Minor:", minor, sizeof(minor)) > 0 &&
+	    !kstrtouint(minor, 10, &m) && m < NVKVM_MAX_GPUS)
+		nvkvm.gpu_minor[idx] = (int)m;
+}
+
 int nvkvm_hostfile_discover_gpus(void)
 {
 	int i, shm_slot, count = 0;
@@ -325,6 +364,7 @@ int nvkvm_hostfile_discover_gpus(void)
 				i);
 			break;
 		}
+		nvkvm_parse_identity(tmp, nbytes, count);
 		count++;
 	}
 
diff --git a/src/guest/nvkvm_uvm_ext.c b/src/guest/nvkvm_uvm_ext.c
index 79c757e..10b2ab2 100644
--- a/src/guest/nvkvm_uvm_ext.c
+++ b/src/guest/nvkvm_uvm_ext.c
@@ -205,24 +205,186 @@ static int uvm_call(struct ext_target t, unsigned int cmd,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * NV_ESC_RM_CONTROL.  Like rm_alloc(), `params` travels in the aux slot and the
+ * stub re-points NVOS54.params at its own copy (nvkvm_stub.c, ptr_off 16 for
+ * nr 0x2a), and the isolate gates `cmd` against the control allowlist exactly
+ * as it does for libcuda's own controls.
+ */
+static int rm_control(struct ext_target t, __u32 h_client, __u32 h_object,
+		      __u32 cmd, void *params, __u32 size, __u32 *nvstatus)
+{
+	struct nvos54_parameters *p;
+	long ret;
+
+	p = kzalloc(sizeof(*p), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!p)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	p->h_client    = h_client;
+	p->h_object    = h_object;
+	p->cmd         = cmd;
+	p->params      = 0;
+	p->params_size = size;
+	ret = nvkvm_virtio_ioctl_on_isolate_nomm(
+			t.isolate_id, t.handle_id, t.session_id,
+			FE_CMD(NV_ESC_RM_CONTROL, struct nvos54_parameters),
+			p, sizeof(*p), params, size);
+	if (ret >= 0)
+		*nvstatus = p->status;
+	kfree(p);
+	return ret < 0 ? (int)ret : 0;
+}
+
+/* The three NV0000 controls ext_owner_gpu() needs, all already in the control
+ * allowlist (0x201, 0x275, 0x205).  Layouts from ctrl0000gpu.h; none has
+ * changed since 515. */
+#define NV0000_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_ATTACHED_IDS          0x00000201u
+#define NV0000_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_UUID_FROM_GPU_ID      0x00000275u
+#define NV0000_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_ID_INFO_V2            0x00000205u
+#define NV0000_CTRL_GPU_MAX_ATTACHED_GPUS             32u
+#define NV0000_CTRL_GPU_INVALID_ID                    0xffffffffu
+#define NV0000_GPU_UUID_FROM_GPU_ID_FORMAT_BINARY     0x2u
+
+struct nv0000_attached_ids { __u32 gpu_ids[NV0000_CTRL_GPU_MAX_ATTACHED_GPUS]; };
+struct nv0000_uuid_from_gpu_id {
+	__u32 gpu_id;
+	__u32 flags;
+	__u8  gpu_uuid[256];
+	__u32 uuid_str_len;
+};
+struct nv0000_id_info_v2 {
+	__u32 gpu_id, gpu_flags, device_instance, sub_device_instance;
+	__u32 sli_status, board_id, gpu_instance;
+	__s32 numa_id;
+};
+
+/*
+ * Which GPU the backing has to be allocated under.
+ *
+ * UVM_MAP_EXTERNAL_ALLOCATION requires the OWNING GPU of the memory to be
+ * registered on the va_space, even for sysmem (uvm_map_external.c,
+ * set_ext_gpu_map_location(): "the owning GPU must have been registered" ->
+ * NV_ERR_INVALID_DEVICE), and the owning GPU of an RM sysmem object is the GPU
+ * of the device it was allocated under.  Mapping it on further registered GPUs
+ * is fine: the peer check there is skipped for sysmem.  So the device is the
+ * GPU of a GPU registered on this fd, never a fixed deviceId 0 --
+ * with that, a process whose only context is on GPU 1 (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1,
+ * or a VM given only the host's second GPU) got rc=999 on every
+ * cuMemAllocManaged.
+ *
+ * Yields RM's deviceInstance for NV01_DEVICE_0 and the /dev/nvidiaN minor
+ * whose fd satisfies the osIsGpuAccessible() check in deviceConstruct.
+ */
+static int ext_owner_gpu(struct nvkvm_uvm_fd_state *st, struct ext_target tctl,
+			 __u32 h_client, __u32 *device_instance, int *minor)
+{
+	struct nv0000_attached_ids *ids = NULL;
+	struct nv0000_uuid_from_gpu_id *u = NULL;
+	struct nv0000_id_info_v2 *info = NULL;
+	struct nvkvm_uvm_gpu_reg *g;
+	struct nvkvm_uvm_vas_reg *v;
+	char want[NVKVM_UUID_STRLEN + 1];
+	__u8 uuid[16];
+	bool have = false;
+	__u32 nvstatus = 0, i;
+	int ret, k;
+
+	/* Prefer a GPU with a VA space: the range is mapped on exactly those
+	 * (ext_collect_uuids), so the owner is then one the process uses. */
+	mutex_lock(&st->lock);
+	list_for_each_entry(v, &st->registered_va_spaces, list) {
+		memcpy(uuid, v->gpu_uuid, sizeof(uuid));
+		have = true;
+		break;
+	}
+	if (!have) {
+		list_for_each_entry(g, &st->registered_gpus, list) {
+			memcpy(uuid, g->gpu_uuid, sizeof(uuid));
+			have = true;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&st->lock);
+	if (!have)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	ids  = kzalloc(sizeof(*ids), GFP_KERNEL);
+	u    = kzalloc(sizeof(*u), GFP_KERNEL);
+	info = kzalloc(sizeof(*info), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!ids || !u || !info) { ret = -ENOMEM; goto out; }
+
+	ret = rm_control(tctl, h_client, h_client, NV0000_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_ATTACHED_IDS,
+			 ids, sizeof(*ids), &nvstatus);
+	if (ret || nvstatus)
+		goto fail;
+	ret = -ENODEV;
+	for (i = 0; i < NV0000_CTRL_GPU_MAX_ATTACHED_GPUS; i++) {
+		if (ids->gpu_ids[i] == NV0000_CTRL_GPU_INVALID_ID)
+			break;
+		memset(u, 0, sizeof(*u));
+		u->gpu_id = ids->gpu_ids[i];
+		u->flags  = NV0000_GPU_UUID_FROM_GPU_ID_FORMAT_BINARY;
+		if (rm_control(tctl, h_client, h_client,
+			       NV0000_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_UUID_FROM_GPU_ID,
+			       u, sizeof(*u), &nvstatus) || nvstatus)
+			continue;
+		if (memcmp(u->gpu_uuid, uuid, sizeof(uuid)))
+			continue;
+		info->gpu_id = ids->gpu_ids[i];
+		ret = rm_control(tctl, h_client, h_client, NV0000_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_ID_INFO_V2,
+				 info, sizeof(*info), &nvstatus);
+		if (ret || nvstatus)
+			goto fail;
+		*device_instance = info->device_instance;
+		break;
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		goto fail;
+
+	/* The node: match the UUID against the host `information` bodies. */
+	snprintf(want, sizeof(want),
+		 "GPU-%02x%02x%02x%02x-%02x%02x-%02x%02x-%02x%02x-%02x%02x%02x%02x%02x%02x",
+		 uuid[0], uuid[1], uuid[2], uuid[3], uuid[4], uuid[5], uuid[6], uuid[7],
+		 uuid[8], uuid[9], uuid[10], uuid[11], uuid[12], uuid[13], uuid[14],
+		 uuid[15]);
+	ret = -ENODEV;
+	for (k = 0; k < nvkvm.num_gpus && k < NVKVM_MAX_GPUS; k++) {
+		if (!strcasecmp(nvkvm.gpu_uuid[k], want) && nvkvm.gpu_minor[k] >= 0) {
+			*minor = nvkvm.gpu_minor[k];
+			ret = 0;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		goto fail;
+	goto out;
+
+fail:
+	pr_warn("nvkvm: uvm fallback: cannot resolve the registered GPU's device (ret=%d nvstatus=0x%x)\n",
+		ret, nvstatus);
+	ret = ret ? ret : -EIO;
+out:
+	kfree(ids); kfree(u); kfree(info);
+	return ret;
+}
+
 /* ── the private RM object tree ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
 
 /*
  * Build the client/device/subdevice tree this UVM fd allocates its backing
- * under.  Called once per UVM fd, under st->ext_lock.
+ * under.  Called once per UVM fd, under st->ext_lock, after libcuda has
+ * registered at least one GPU (the managed mmap that triggers this follows
+ * UVM_REGISTER_GPU).
  *
- * Two things here are load-bearing and were established by measurement
- * (tools/uvm_sysmem_probe.c on 575.51.03 / RTX 3060), not from the SDK:
+ * Load-bearing, established by measurement (tools/uvm_sysmem_probe.c on
+ * 575.51.03 / RTX 3060) and by reading deviceConstruct():
  *
  *  - NV01_DEVICE_0 is refused with NV_ERR_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS (0x1b)
- *    unless a /dev/nvidiaN fd has been bound to the client's control fd with
- *    NV_ESC_REGISTER_FD first.  That is the only reason a device handle is
- *    opened at all; nothing else is ever issued on it.
- *  - deviceId 0 is used unconditionally.  The object is *system* memory, so it
- *    is not tied to the GPU whose device it is allocated under — UVM dups it
- *    into whichever GPU MAP_EXTERNAL_ALLOCATION names, and cross-device dup of
- *    a sysmem object is exactly what nvUvmInterfaceDupMemory does for
- *    cudaMalloc today.  The device is an allocation context, not a placement.
+ *    unless the calling process holds an fd for THAT GPU's /dev/nvidiaN
+ *    (osIsGpuAccessible -> nv_is_gpu_accessible iterates the caller's files).
+ *    That is the only reason a device handle is opened at all; it is also
+ *    bound with NV_ESC_REGISTER_FD as before.  Nothing else is issued on it.
+ *  - the device is a registered GPU's (ext_owner_gpu() says why).
  */
 static int ext_tree_build(struct nvkvm_uvm_fd_state *st)
 {
@@ -230,8 +392,9 @@ static int ext_tree_build(struct nvkvm_uvm_fd_state *st)
 	struct nv2080_alloc_parameters *sp = NULL;
 	struct nv_ioctl_register_fd *rp = NULL;
 	struct ext_target tctl, tdev;
-	__u32 nvstatus = 0;
+	__u32 nvstatus = 0, device_instance = 0;
 	__u32 h;
+	int minor = -1;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (st->ext_ready)
@@ -243,20 +406,35 @@ static int ext_tree_build(struct nvkvm_uvm_fd_state *st)
 		st->ext_ctl = NULL;
 		return ret;
 	}
-	st->ext_dev = nvkvm_fd_ctx_open_dev(NVKVM_DEV_GPU(0), O_RDWR);
-	if (IS_ERR(st->ext_dev)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(st->ext_dev);
-		st->ext_dev = NULL;
-		goto err;
-	}
 	tctl = ext_target_of(st->ext_ctl);
-	tdev = ext_target_of(st->ext_dev);
 
 	rp = kzalloc(sizeof(*rp), GFP_KERNEL);
 	dp = kzalloc(sizeof(*dp), GFP_KERNEL);
 	sp = kzalloc(sizeof(*sp), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!rp || !dp || !sp) { ret = -ENOMEM; goto err; }
 
+	h = RM_HANDLE_LET_RM_CHOOSE;
+	ret = rm_alloc(tctl, 0, 0, &h, NV01_ROOT, NULL, 0, &nvstatus);
+	if (ret || nvstatus) {
+		pr_warn("nvkvm: uvm fallback: NV01_ROOT ret=%d nvstatus=0x%x\n",
+			ret, nvstatus);
+		ret = ret ? ret : -EIO;
+		goto err;
+	}
+	st->ext_h_client = h;
+
+	ret = ext_owner_gpu(st, tctl, st->ext_h_client, &device_instance, &minor);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err;
+
+	st->ext_dev = nvkvm_fd_ctx_open_dev(NVKVM_DEV_GPU(minor), O_RDWR);
+	if (IS_ERR(st->ext_dev)) {
+		ret = PTR_ERR(st->ext_dev);
+		st->ext_dev = NULL;
+		goto err;
+	}
+	tdev = ext_target_of(st->ext_dev);
+
 	/* Bind the device fd to the control fd.  The field carries a QEMU
 	 * handle_id, not an fd — the stub resolves it (nvkvm_stub.c, nr 0xc9). */
 	rp->ctl_fd = (__s32)st->ext_ctl->handle_id;
@@ -269,17 +447,7 @@ static int ext_tree_build(struct nvkvm_uvm_fd_state *st)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	h = RM_HANDLE_LET_RM_CHOOSE;
-	ret = rm_alloc(tctl, 0, 0, &h, NV01_ROOT, NULL, 0, &nvstatus);
-	if (ret || nvstatus) {
-		pr_warn("nvkvm: uvm fallback: NV01_ROOT ret=%d nvstatus=0x%x\n",
-			ret, nvstatus);
-		ret = ret ? ret : -EIO;
-		goto err;
-	}
-	st->ext_h_client = h;
-
-	dp->device_id      = 0;
+	dp->device_id      = device_instance;
 	dp->h_client_share = st->ext_h_client;
 	h = RM_HANDLE_LET_RM_CHOOSE;
 	ret = rm_alloc(tctl, st->ext_h_client, st->ext_h_client, &h,
@@ -430,21 +598,26 @@ void nvkvm_uvm_ext_release(struct nvkvm_mmap_region *region)
 /* ── the synthesis ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
 
 /*
- * The GPUs this va_space has registered.  gpuAttributesCount == 0 does NOT mean
- * "all GPUs" — UVM refuses it outright (uvm_map_external.c:993-994) — so the
- * set has to come from what UVM_REGISTER_GPU told us.
+ * The GPUs to map the range on.  gpuAttributesCount == 0 does NOT mean "all
+ * GPUs" — UVM refuses it outright (uvm_map_external.c:993-994) — and a GPU
+ * that is merely REGISTERED is not enough either: every entry is looked up with
+ * uvm_va_space_get_gpu_by_uuid_with_gpu_va_space() and one without a GPU VA
+ * space fails the whole call with NV_ERR_INVALID_DEVICE.  libcuda registers
+ * every visible GPU but creates a GPU VA space only per context, so with two
+ * GPUs visible and one context the registered set was wrong.  Use what
+ * UVM_REGISTER_GPU_VASPACE told us.
  */
 static __u32 ext_collect_uuids(struct nvkvm_uvm_fd_state *st, void *mp,
 			       size_t mp_size)
 {
-	struct nvkvm_uvm_gpu_reg *g;
+	struct nvkvm_uvm_vas_reg *g;
 	__u32 n = 0;
 
 	/* The writer uses st->lock.  We arrive with ext_lock held, establishing
